docs {
  # Fantadex API
  
  Applies a trusted `Origin` header to every request. better-auth enforces a
  CSRF origin check on cookie-bearing requests, and the Bruno client keeps a
  cookie jar — so without this header, sign-in after another session's cookie
  is set would fail with "Missing or null Origin". Mobile clients using bearer
  tokens (no cookies) are unaffected.
  
  `baseUrl` is a collection variable and already includes the `/api` base path.
  
  ## Getting started
  1. Seed the database from the backend: `pnpm seed` (creates
     `admin@fantadex.io`, password `Password123!`, as an admin).
  2. Select the `Local` environment (top-right).
  3. Run `1-Auth > Sign In` (saves `token`, used by every authed request).
  4. Create countries (`2-Countries`) + fanta (`3-Fanta`), then explore
     `4-Tastings`. `5-Session` (Get Session / Sign Out) runs last.
  
  Folders are numbered so a full collection run (`bru run`) executes in order —
  Sign Out lives in `5-Session` so it doesn't invalidate the token mid-run.
}
